(ns allgo.astro.cio-data
  "The IAU 2006/2000A series for the celestial intermediate pole's
  coordinates X and Y and for the CIO locator s (as s + XY/2), the IERS
  Conventions (2010) tables 5.2a, 5.2b and 5.2d, taken from ERFA -- the
  BSD-licensed release of the IAU's SOFA library -- whose copyright notice,
  conditions and disclaimer head this file.

  Each frequency is its fourteen fundamental-argument multipliers (l, l',
  F, D, Omega, the mean longitudes of Mercury through Neptune, and the
  general precession p_A) with its terms, each [xy sc power amplitude]:
  xy 0 for X and 1 for Y, sc 0 for the sine and 1 for the cosine, the
  power of T it multiplies, and its amplitude in microarcseconds.")

